FILAMENT APOCALYPSE — 25s GROUNDED CUT

(25s · 8K UHD · 30fps · 2.39:1 · Surreal Mythic Realism)

GROUND PHYSICS — GLOBAL (APPLIES TO ALL SCENES)

Ground behaves like thick liquid ink / viscous paint

Each lion footstep:

Compresses the surface

Pushes ink outward

Leaves raised filament ridges

Ink slowly flows back after contact

No hovering, no sliding, no skating

Visible weight transfer heel → pad → toe

Dust + ink micro-splatter on push-off

SCENE-BY-SCENE SCRIPT
SCENE 1 — ANCHOR (0.0–1.0s | 1.0s)

Visual:
Still anchor. Three lions mid-step.
Front paws fully planted, ink pooled around pads.

Ground:
Ink compressed downward, slight outward bulge.

Camera: Locked

SCENE 2 (1.0–2.8s | 1.8s)

Visual:
First step forward.
Front paw presses deep → ink ripples outward in slow waves.

Camera: Low forward dolly (35mm anamorphic)
Key fix: Visible resistance as paw pushes ground back

SCENE 3 (2.8–4.5s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Rear paw lifts — ink stretches upward into threads before snapping back.

Ground:
Elastic filament recoil, tiny droplets fling outward.

Camera: Slight parallax shift

SCENE 4 (4.5–6.2s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Second step cycle begins.
Multiple paws land out of phase, creating overlapping ink waves.

Sky: Still intact, tension building
Camera: Smooth push

SCENE 5 (6.2–7.8s | 1.6s)

Visual:
First sky filament stretch.
Ground remains heavy and stable — contrast emphasized.

Ground:
Ink ridges accumulate behind footprints.

SCENE 6 (7.8–9.6s | 1.8s)

Visual:
Large filament sheet peels from sky.
Lion steps sink slightly deeper as pressure increases.

Camera: Wider (24mm)
Effect: Weight feels heavier

SCENE 7 (9.6–11.3s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Sky collapse accelerates.
Ink ground shudders; concentric ripples radiate from each paw strike.

Camera: Subtle instability
FX: Ink splash micro-strands on impact

SCENE 8 (11.3–13.0s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Particles freeze mid-air.
Lions still moving — paws actively displacing frozen ink.

Key moment:
Ground deforms even while air is frozen → dominance

SCENE 9 (13.0–14.7s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Time resumes.
Ink snaps back violently around lifted paws.

Camera: Tight low angle on legs
Detail: Muscle-driven push-off visible

SCENE 10 (14.7–16.4s | 1.7s)

Visual:
Sky nearly gone.
Ink ground begins thinning into filament strands near horizon.

Camera: Forward, steady

SCENE 11 (16.4–18.2s | 1.8s)

Visual:
Final sky collapse. Void revealed.
Ink ground calms but remains thick under lions.

Camera: Hard stop → locked

SCENE 12 (18.2–20.0s | 1.8s)

Visual:
Lions continue walking into emptiness.
Each step leaves deep, sculpted ink footprints.

Sound implied: Dull, heavy impact

SCENE 13 (20.0–22.0s | 2.0s)

Visual:
Close-up tracking of footprints behind them.
Ink slowly flows inward but never fully erases.

Camera: Low trailing dolly

SCENE 14 — FINAL FRAME (22.0–25.0s | 3.0s)

Visual:
Footprints dissolve into fine filament dust.
Ground finally still. No sky. No motion.

Camera: Absolute stillness
End: Silence